    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d198">

                <pb facs="0316" n="204" xml:id="pg204"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.77/1670</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Vice President of the American International
                        Corp</hi>. (<hi rendition="#italic">R. P. Tinsley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 9, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose to the
                    Department, for its information and the Department’s archives, copies of certain
                    correspondence from the Siems-Carey Railway &amp; Canal Co. in Peking, relative
                    to the cessation on account of disturbed political conditions of the railway
                    surveys in China which were being carried out in pursuance of a contract with
                    the Chinese Government. With this correspondence will be found a memorandum from
                    the corporation’s attorney regarding the status of the railway work as a result
                    of the cessation of the surveys.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d198-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">R. P. Tinsley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d198-a1.xml" xpointer="d198-a1"/>
